          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "negah dâshtan is \"to hold in view\": negah, \"look\", with dâshtan, \"to hold\". Both are native; negah is usually traced to Middle Persian nigāh. dâshtan, \"to have\", is an inherited verb; it is usually traced to Middle Persian dāštan, \"to hold\"."
